     "source": "In-game destination screen (8 Oct 2026); Redirection is confirmed as a map condition in the official Frozen Trail 2.0 notes.",
     "caveat": "The steps and loot below come from early-access community reports and may change. No drop rates are published, and none are given here.",
     "guide": [
      {
       "title": "Find a Damaged Emperor Relay",
       "text": "Several relays appear across the map during Redirection. Players report a red beam and a relay icon marking each one.",
       "status": "REPORTED"
      },
      {
       "title": "Search it for an Emperor Beacon",
       "text": "Searching a relay is reported to give an Emperor Beacon. Players report carrying up to three.",
       "status": "REPORTED"
      },
      {
       "title": "Deploy the beacon under open sky",
       "text": "Place it somewhere with a clear view of the sky. The beacon beam is reported to be visible map-wide, so expect other squads to come looking.",
       "status": "REPORTED"
      },
      {
       "title": "Take cover from the falling payload",
       "text": "The payload comes down with debris that can hurt health and shields. Stay clear until it lands.",
       "status": "REPORTED"
      },
      {
       "title": "Breach the payload, then sweep the debris",
       "text": "The payload is reported to hold ARC Couplers (Conductive, Insulated and Plated) plus other ARC parts. Smaller debris reportedly drops ARC materials such as ARC Alloy, ARC Circuitry and ARC Motion Cores. Contents vary per payload.",
       "status": "REPORTED",
       "items": [
        "arc-alloy",
        "arc-circuitry",
        "arc-motion-core"
       ]
      },
      {
       "title": "Craft the Emperor Gateway Conduit",
       "text": "Community guides report the conduit is crafted at Workbench I from one of each coupler plus the Emperor Gateway Conduit Blueprint.",
       "status": "REPORTED"
      },
      {
       "title": "Enter the Fallen Emperor",
       "text": "The conduit is reported to open the way into the Fallen Emperor. Embark confirms only that an Emperor has fallen, that rare technology lies inside, and that Raiders must find a way in.",
       "status": "REPORTED"
      }
     ]
